  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan\rBlock Plan\r2025.09-D1 EXISTING AND PROPOSED PLANS\rNoise Assessment of a New Kitchen Extract System 2/10/25\rHighway Safety Impact form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external works shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible in colour and texture to those used in the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved plans.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The premises shall only be open for business between the hours of\r\r10:00 and 23:00 Monday to Sunday (including Bank Holidays) \r\rand all activity associated with the use shall cease within 1 hour of the closing time specified above. \r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r",
    "No occupation of the development shall take place until an Odour Assessment must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority which demonstrates that residents will not be negatively impacted by odour from the ground floor restaurant.\r\rReason: To protect future residents from odour\r",
    "No occupation of the development shall take place until an acoustic report, written in line with the methodology in BS4142:2014+A1 2019, has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. The report must set out the sound level generated from the kitchen extraction system and state the noise control measures to be employed to ensure the noise from the system does not exceed a level of 5dB below the typical measured background noise level measured as L(A)90 15 minutes during operational hours, at the façade of the nearest or most noise affected residential property.\r\rReason: To protect the local amenity from noise and disturbance\r"
  ],
